"The prognosis is based on favorable pathological findings, including an ISUP grade group 1 (Gleason 3+3) and negative surgical margins with no seminal vesicle invasion or lymphovascular invasion. The preoperative PSA was low at 2.11 ng/mL. A key limitation is the absence of nodal sampling; therefore, pNx status cannot be definitively classified as pN0, which widens prognostic uncertainty. Biopsy-to-prostatectomy differences are not documented for comparison. Prognostic revision would significantly benefit from postoperative PSA measurements and tracking its subsequent trajectory. The current data provides a limited picture regarding local recurrence risk due to the missing nodal assessment. The fixed estimated horizon is 93.67 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 60.89–126.46 months; its coverage has not been validated."
